{% comment %}
  The ASCII backdrop. Reads a generated field from _data/ascii/ and stacks its
  layers back to front; depth, opacity and parallax are handled in CSS/JS.

  Params:
    field  key under site.data.ascii (default: bosch_field)

  The artwork is decorative, so the whole field is hidden from assistive tech and
  from the pointer. It is real text, escaped at render time, so any character in
  the source data is safe to use.

  Every layer is prefixed with a newline. An HTML parser drops exactly one
  newline after <pre>, so this guarantees each layer's first row lands on the same
  line whether or not its own top row happens to be blank — without which the
  layers slide a row out of register.
{% endcomment %}

{% capture ascii_newline %}
{% endcapture %}

{% assign field_key = include.field | default: 'bosch_field' %}
{% assign field = site.data.ascii[field_key] %}

{% if field %}
  <div class="ascii-field" data-ascii-field aria-hidden="true" role="presentation">
    {% for layer in field.layers %}
      <pre
        class="ascii-field__layer ascii-field__layer--{{ layer.id }}"
        data-ascii-layer="{{ layer.id }}"
        data-depth="{{ forloop.index }}"
        style="--ascii-columns: {{ field.columns }}; --ascii-rows: {{ field.rows }}"
      >{{ layer.art | escape | prepend: ascii_newline }}</pre>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
{% endif %}
